From f595dda06ed99be458db6354eec7b93ec295c87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] param-spec, rend-spec: Document HSDir DoS parameters

Add the "HSDirFetchBudgetPercent", "HSDirFetchShedding" and
"HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop" consensus parameters, and note that
HSV3MaxDescriptorSize also bounds the request body a non-authority
directory server will buffer. In rend-spec, state that each descriptor
fetch and upload is made on its own circuit, that HSDirs may close or
refuse requests that break this or come from an unknown previous hop, or
shed fetches while overloaded, and that clients should then try another
HSDir.

Companion to tor#41339.
---
 spec/param-spec.md              | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md | 10 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spec/param-spec.md b/spec/param-spec.md
index 6a86178f..e653dbeb 100644
--- a/spec/param-spec.md
+++ b/spec/param-spec.md
@@ -347,6 +347,11 @@ will upload its descriptor to.
 Min: 1. Max: 128. Default: 4
 
 "HSV3MaxDescriptorSize" -- Maximum descriptor size (in bytes).
+On relays that are not directory authorities, this also bounds the body of
+an HTTP request that the directory server will buffer: once a request body
+reaches this many bytes (or 16 MB, if that is smaller), the request is
+rejected before more of it is buffered. Directory authorities keep the
+16 MB limit.
 Min: 1. Max: INT32_MAX. Default: 50000
 
 "hs_service_max_rdv_failures" -- This parameter determines the
@@ -492,6 +497,38 @@ First appeared: 0.4.9.0-alpha-dev.
     First appeared: 0.4.9.0-alpha-dev.
 ```
 
+"HSDirFetchBudgetPercent" -- The budget of "HSDirFetchShedding": the
+onion service descriptor bytes a directory may be asked for in a second, as
+a percentage of the lower of the directory's configured bandwidth rate and
+its observed bandwidth. Each fetch counts as the size of the descriptor it
+asks for. The budget is at least 512 KBytes per second. A nonzero relay
+torrc option "HSDirFetchBudget" replaces it with a fixed number of bytes
+per second.
+Min: 1. Max: 100. Default: 50.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
+"HSDirFetchShedding" -- If 1, a public onion service directory that is
+asked for more onion service descriptor bytes in a second than its budget
+(see "HSDirFetchBudgetPercent") sheds some descriptor fetches by closing
+their circuits with reason RESOURCELIMIT. In each second after one over the
+budget, it answers first, up to half the budget, the fetches of descriptors
+fetched no more often than a per-descriptor rate, and the others at random;
+it never answers more than one and a half times the budget in a second.
+Below the budget it refuses no fetch. Directories count such fetches
+whatever the value. The relay torrc option of the same name (0, 1, or auto)
+overrides this parameter.
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
+"HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop" -- If 1, a public onion service directory
+refuses, with an HTTP 503 response, an onion service descriptor fetch or
+upload whose previous hop is not a relay in its consensus or for which it
+has a descriptor. Directories count such requests whatever the value. The
+relay torrc option of the same name (0, 1, or auto) overrides this
+parameter. It is independent of "refuseunknownexits".
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
 <a id="param-spec.txt-10"></a>
 
 ## Padding-related parameters {#padding}
diff --git a/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md b/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
index 066f34d4..74f72e98 100644
--- a/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
+++ b/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
@@ -433,6 +433,16 @@ version which is "3" in this case.
 
 These requests must be made anonymously, on circuits not used for
 anything else.
+Each descriptor fetch and each descriptor upload MUST be made on its own
+circuit: a client or service MUST NOT send a second such request on a
+circuit that already carried one.
+An onion service directory MAY close a circuit that carries more than one
+such request, and MAY refuse a request whose previous hop it does not
+recognize as a relay (see "HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop" in the
+[parameter specification](../param-spec.md)).
+It MAY also close the circuit of a descriptor fetch while it is asked for
+more descriptor bytes than it can serve (see "HSDirFetchShedding").
+Clients SHOULD then try another responsible onion service directory.
 
